        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0651" n="567" sameAs="frus:frus1886/pg567"/>

                <head>No. 295.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Jackson to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 2, 1885</date>.
                        (Received December 11.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 117.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In accordance with the instruction
                    contained in your No. 87, of November 13, I have addressed a note to Mr.
                    Mariscal directing his attention to the prohibitory character of the import
                    duties placed by the existing tariff laws of Mexico upon certain food products
                    of the United States, and suggesting such modifications as will rather invite
                    than exclude them. I have the honor to inclose a copy of my note.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HENEY R. JACKSON.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d299-a1.xml" xpointer="d299-a1"/>
            </div>
